From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:33:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Embedding: a repeated compare sets the flags when it ends

REPE CMPS, REPNE CMPS, REPE SCAS and REPNE SCAS set the flags of their
last element's compare when they finish. A fault, an interrupt or a
single-step trap between two elements shows the flags the instruction
started with. The embedded loops set the flags of every element, which
the frame of such a stop showed.

They now test each element with ordinary arithmetic, which leaves the
host's condition flags, the guest's, alone, keep the last operands in
the frame (Embedder.StringOperands) and set the flags when the loop
ends.
